.TH HERDSMAN 1 "" "herdsman" "herdsman manual"
.SH NAME
herdsman \- run a team of coding agents inside herdr
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
herdsman: run a team of coding agents inside herdr.

Usage:
  herdsman web [--port 7878] [--host <ip>] [--allow-host <name>]... [--inbox <folder>]
               [--client <url>|none] [--public-url <https url>] [--session <name>]
               [--route <folder>]... [--open] [--no-qr]
  herdsman <command> [args]   (the commands below)
  herdsman version
  herdsman help

Commands:
  web      Serve the web app and print its URL, with a one-run token, and a QR code.
           It listens on 127.0.0.1 unless --host names one other address,
           such as a LAN or Tailscale IP, to open it from a phone. The app is
           also hosted at https://herdsman.arafat.ai (--client) and reaches this
           server across origins; every browser still pairs with a code
           printed here. A phone can use the hosted app only through HTTPS:
           with --public-url (for example the address of tailscale serve),
           the QR code opens the hosted app.
  afk      Print how long the user has been away: machine idle time or the newest message, whichever is newer.
  approval-gate Bind a relayed go before its effect: approval-gate consume ... | complete <request-id> <outcome>.
  checkpointer Checkpoint the orchestrator's memory and compact it: TARGET=<pane> checkpointer [--once|--probe] | checkpointer guard <name> <pane>.
  commit   Commit a worktree with a Conventional Commits message.
  config   Read and change the configuration; install the shell integration.
  cost     Report measured tokens and cost per task, project or route.
  daemon   The per-user message channel daemon: run|install|uninstall|start|stop|restart|status|route|setup|pair|credential.
  delete   Remove a route, once a verified snapshot makes that undoable.
  diff     Show a worktree's changes.
  doctor   Check that this machine can run a route: herdr, gh, the binary, the inbox, the sandbox, the load.
  each     Run a command in every worktree.
  eval     Report a suite's runs with intervals and an A/A control (experimental).
  export   Copy the whole account to a new folder.
  go       Enter a worktree.
  hook     Show, approve or run a worktree hook.
  import   Rebuild an account from an export.
  ls       List the repository's worktrees.
  mcp      Serve the daemon's services as MCP tools over stdio.
  message  The adjutant message channel: message status|wait|read|release|ack|send|hold|unhold, and register|courier|card-watch|resume-goal|authority|leak-gate.
  models   Probe each installed harness: its version, models, efforts and default effort as it reports them.
  new      Make a task's branch and worktree.
  pause    Interrupt a route's agents and hold its channel; every pane stays open.
  plugin   Manage plugins (experimental).
  project  Work on a project's context repo: project context init|check|note, project log.
  recommend The same as suggest.
  resource Record a resource a task created: resource add.
  resume   Continue a paused route, or restart a stopped one from its record.
  review   Prepare a reviewer: herdsman review start --worktree <path> --head <commit>.
  route    Check a route folder (route check) or append a run-state line (route log).
  run-check Run one heavy check at a time on this machine, behind a load gate (--publish <hours>: the load reading).
  spec     Print the SDK contracts: spec cli|proto|descriptor.
  status   Print a health snapshot of every agent in HERDSMAN_STATUS_SPECS and of the machine.
  stop     End a route's sessions and service panes; the work stays on disk.
  suggest  Search the catalog of tips and tools.
  teardown Stop what a task runs, keeping what it holds.
  trace    Show or export one route's spans as OpenTelemetry.
  transcript-audit Audit a Claude or Codex transcript for writes: transcript-audit claude|codex <transcript> <session-id> [root/ ...].
  undo     Restore a snapshot.
  up       Start a route: workspace, private inbox, both coordinators, the pair and the first brief.
  update   Install the latest signed release over this binary.
  wait     Wait for the next event of the loop (a report, a review, a blocked or stalled agent, a health flag), or TICK.
  watch    Watch implementers, the reviewer or pull requests: herdsman watch implementers|reviewer|prs.
  version  Print the version.
  help     Print this help.
.fi
